  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-93115",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, let's approximate the weight of the cake Grant ate to the nearest hundred:\n\n$$\n745⟶700\n$$\n\nThe ratio of the weight of Grant's portion to the weight of Stephanie's portion is \n\n$$\n\\frac{7}{3}.\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe numerator represents the weight of Grant's  part and the denominator represents  the weight of Stephanies part.\n\nWe can make a numerator of $700$ by multiplying the numerator and denominator by \n $100:$\n\n$$\n\\frac{7\\times 100}{3\\times 100}=\\frac{700}{300}\n$$\n\nTherefore, Stephanie ate approximately $300$ grams of cake.",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
